= AlbumType2 Template Documentation =
This template creates a standardized layout for album pages: a cover card with the album details, and tabs for the tracklist, cover art, shops/downloads, streaming and crossfade previews. It is rendered by [[Module:Album]].

Each album is also listed in the page's table of contents (under the nearest heading), so readers can jump straight to it.

== Usage ==
<pre>
{{AlbumType2
|albumtitle=
|officialromtitle=
|singers=
|datereleased=
|label=
|albumartist=
|image=
|intro=

|t1title=
|t1info=
|t1singers=
|t1lyricist=
|t1composer=
|t1arranger=

|t2title=
|t2lyricist=
|t2composer=

|shops=
|jpshops=
|streams=
|spotifyalbumid=
|crossfadeyt=
|crossfadennd=
|notes=
}}
</pre>

== Parameters ==
=== Basic Information Parameters ===
{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Description !! Required? !! Example
|-
| albumtitle || The title of the album || Yes || <code>My Album Title</code>
|-
| officialjaptitle / officialromtitle / officialengtitle || Official Japanese, romanized and English titles. The romanized and English ones are shown under the title || No || <code>Yumeiro Signal</code>
|-
| singers || Featured artists on the album || No || <code>Artist A, Artist B</code>
|-
| datereleased || Release date of the album || Yes || <code>July 07, 2024</code>
|-
| label || Record label or publisher || No || <code>Universal Music</code>
|-
| catalognumber || Catalog number || No || <code>LGIN-1234</code>
|-
| albumartist || Artist who created the album artwork || No || <code>Cover Artist Name</code>
|-
| image || Filename of the album cover image || No || <code>Album_cover.jpg</code>
|-
| imagealt, imagealt2 &hellip; imagealt4 || Alternate covers (limited editions etc.). Shown next to the main cover in the '''Cover Art''' tab || No || <code>Album_cover_limited.jpg</code>
|-
| gallery || Extra content for the '''Cover Art''' tab || No || <code><nowiki><gallery>...</gallery></nowiki></code>
|-
| suppressacg || <code>true</code> hides the '''Cover Art''' tab || No || <code>true</code>
|}

=== Text Around the Album ===
{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Where it appears !! Example
|-
| intro || Under the cover card, above the tabs || <code>First full album, released for the 10th anniversary.</code>
|-
| notes || Below the tabs || <code>* Limited edition includes a DVD.</code>
|-
| tsp (or tracksectionprefix) || Inside the Tracklist tab, before the tracklist || <code><nowiki><h4>CD</h4></nowiki></code>
|-
| tss (or tracksectionsuffix) || Inside the Tracklist tab, after the tracklist || <code><nowiki>'''Bonus DVD:''' ...</nowiki></code>
|}

=== Table of Contents ===
{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Description !! Default
|-
| toctitle || Text of the album's entry in the table of contents || The album title, without ruby readings or links
|-
| headinglevel || Heading level of that entry (2&ndash;6). Use 4 when the album sits under a level-3 heading || <code>3</code>
|-
| notoc || <code>yes</code> leaves the album out of the table of contents || &mdash;
|}

=== Track Parameters ===
Tracks are numbered parameters: <code>t1&hellip;</code> for track 1, <code>t2&hellip;</code> for track 2, and so on. Tracks are listed in number order, and a gap in the numbers is fine. Columns only appear when at least one track uses them.
{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Description !! Example
|-
| t''N''title || Song title (required for the track to show) || <code>Song Title</code> or <code><nowiki><ruby>星空<rt>ほしぞら</rt></ruby></nowiki></code>
|-
| t''N''info || Short extra info after the title || <code>Instrumental</code> or <code><nowiki>{{yt|dQw4w9WgXcQ}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| t''N''singers (or t''N''utaite) || Track singers. Defaults to the page's singer when empty || <code>Artist Name</code>
|-
| t''N''lyricist || Lyric writer || <code>Lyricist Name</code>
|-
| t''N''composer || Music composer || <code>Composer Name</code>
|-
| t''N''arranger || Music arranger || <code>Arranger Name</code>
|-
| t''N''length || Track length || <code>4:16</code>
|-
| t''N''otherprod || Other production credits, shown under the title || <code>Bass: Name · Mix: Name</code>
|-
| t''N''group || Disc or edition the track belongs to. Consecutive tracks with the same group become a titled section (e.g. a bonus DVD) || <code>Bonus DVD</code>
|-
| t''N''bonus / t''N''hidden || <code>true</code> adds a '''Bonus''' / '''Hidden''' badge || <code>true</code>
|-
| t''N''n || Number to display instead of ''N'' (the order still follows ''N'') || <code>B</code> or <code>18-A</code>
|}

The older forms still work: <code>track1title</code>&hellip; parameters, and <code><nowiki>|track={{Track|1|title=...}}</nowiki></code>. New albums should use the <code>t''N''</code> parameters.

=== Media Player Parameters ===
{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Description !! Format !! Example
|-
| spotifyalbumid || Spotify album ID for embedded player || Spotify album ID || <code>3y5m8YvNm0yGHYoi4ada4V</code>
|-
| crossfadeyt || YouTube crossfade preview ID || YouTube video ID || <code>7oYbEQ1_pjg</code>
|-
| crossfadennd || Niconico crossfade preview ID || Niconico video ID || <code>sm20071610</code>
|-
| ytxfddesc || YouTube crossfade description || Text || <code>Album Crossfade</code>
|-
| nndxfddesc || Niconico crossfade description || Text || <code>Album Crossfade</code>
|}

=== Shop Section Types ===
{| class="wikitable"
! Section !! Parameter !! Description !! Example
|-
| International Shops || shops || Links to international stores || <code><nowiki>{{LType2|amazon|149104}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| Japan Only || jpshops || Links to Japanese stores || <code><nowiki>{{LType2|amazon|149104}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| Streaming Services || streams || Links to streaming platforms || <code><nowiki>{{LType2|spotify|3y5m8YvNm0yGHYoi4ada4V}}</nowiki></code>
|}

=== Display Options ===
{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Description !! Values
|-
| groupstyle || How t''N''group is shown. Chosen automatically: sections when each group is one run of tracks, otherwise a badge per track || <code>section</code>, <code>badge</code>, <code>column</code>
|-
| tablefilter || Search and paging for long tracklists (automatic above 15 tracks) || <code>always</code>, <code>never</code>
|}

== Examples ==

=== Basic Usage ===
<pre>
{{AlbumType2
|albumtitle=Album Name
|singers=Artist Name
|datereleased=January 1, 2024
|label=Label Name
|t1title=Song Title
|t1singers=Artist
}}
</pre>
Output:
{{AlbumType2
|albumtitle=Album Name
|singers=Artist Name
|datereleased=January 1, 2024
|label=Label Name
|t1title=Song Title
|t1singers=Artist
|notoc=yes
}}

=== Discs, Lengths and Extra Credits ===
<pre>
{{AlbumType2
|albumtitle=<ruby>星空<rt>ほしぞら</rt></ruby>オーケストラ
|officialromtitle=Hoshizora Orchestra
|datereleased=July 7, 2024
|intro=Second album, with a bonus DVD in the limited edition.
|t1title=Summer Song
|t1info=Single
|t1lyricist=Writer A
|t1composer=Writer A
|t1arranger=Arranger A
|t1length=4:16
|t1group=CD

|t2title=Night Song
|t2composer=Composer B
|t2otherprod=Guitar: Guitarist A · Mix: Engineer A
|t2length=3:58
|t2group=CD

|t3title=Summer Song (Music Video)
|t3bonus=true
|t3group=Bonus DVD
|notes=* The DVD is only included in the limited edition.
}}
</pre>
Output:
{{AlbumType2
|albumtitle=<ruby>星空<rt>ほしぞら</rt></ruby>オーケストラ
|officialromtitle=Hoshizora Orchestra
|datereleased=July 7, 2024
|intro=Second album, with a bonus DVD in the limited edition.
|t1title=Summer Song
|t1info=Single
|t1lyricist=Writer A
|t1composer=Writer A
|t1arranger=Arranger A
|t1length=4:16
|t1group=CD
|t2title=Night Song
|t2composer=Composer B
|t2otherprod=Guitar: Guitarist A · Mix: Engineer A
|t2length=3:58
|t2group=CD
|t3title=Summer Song (Music Video)
|t3bonus=true
|t3group=Bonus DVD
|notes=* The DVD is only included in the limited edition.
|notoc=yes
}}

== Notes ==
* Track titles support line breaks using <nowiki><br /></nowiki>
* Japanese text can be annotated with readings using <nowiki><ruby></nowiki> tags
* Crossfade previews are only shown when video IDs are provided
* The Shops & Downloads, Streaming and Cover Art tabs only appear when they have content

